Additional terms under AGPLv3 section 7(b)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Pursuant to AGPLv3 section 7(b), every covered work, modified or
unmodified, source or object form, MUST preserve the author and
project attribution set out in the NOTICE file in this repository.

The attribution must remain visible in:

  (i)   the source distribution (the NOTICE file itself);
  (ii)  the accompanying documentation;
  (iii) the user-visible interfaces of running instances, including
        (where applicable) "About"/"Version" screens, startup
        banners, command-line `--version` and `--help` output, and
        the interactive network interfaces served to remote users
        as required by AGPLv3 section 13.

This is a non-removable additional term within the meaning of
AGPLv3 section 7. It may not be stripped, obscured, or relocated
to a position that diminishes its visibility when redistributing
or modifying this program. The NOTICE file itself must be preserved
unmodified except for additions consistent with AGPLv3 section 7.

